    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="4">
        <head>Af Rb 4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="16" ed="#liebermann"/>V. Be hlafordsearwe.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Rubrics-Af_4.lnote.oe.5"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-ot-frag"><pb n="16" ed="#liebermann"/>… fordsearwe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-g-prol"><pb n="16" ed="#liebermann"/>V. Be hlafordsearwe.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="17" ed="#liebermann"/>V. Be hlafordsearwe(-swice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Rubrics-Af_4.lnote.oe.6"/>).</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="4" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="17" ed="#liebermann"/>De<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Rubrics-Af_4.lnote.oe.4"/> proditione domini.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="186" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>V Be hlafordsearwe</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="186" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Be cynincges swicdome</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="17" ed="#liebermann"/>Vom Verrath am Herrn.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Rubrics-Af_4.lnote.de.1"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of treachery against one’s lord.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="187" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Concerning treason to one’s lord</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="187" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>Concerning treachery to the king</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_4.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">17</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">De morte regis vel [et <hi rend="italic">Brti</hi>] cuiuslibet domini <hi rend="italic">Hk Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">De morte regis vel [et Brti] cuiuslibet domini Hk Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_4.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">16</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-syrwe <hi rend="italic">Ld;</hi> -syrwungum <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-syrwe Ld; -syrwungum So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_4.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">17</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">übergeschr. vom Schreiber</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written above by the scribe</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rubrics-Af_4.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">40</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Hs. So setzt Plural. — Hs. Hcor setzt ein im Mittelengl. fortlebendes Wort statt des aussterbenden. — Quadr spät. Rezension übersetzt hier (und öfter im folgenden, wo ich es nicht immer bemerke) nicht aus der Agsächs. Rubrik, sondern formt eine Überschrift aus seinem Quadr-Texte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">MS So has the plural. — MS Hcor substitutes a word that lived on in Middle English for the one that was dying out. — Quadr’s later recension does not translate here (or often in what follows, where I do not always note it) from the Anglo-Saxon rubric, but forms a heading from its own Quadr text</seg></note>
      </div>
